{"type":"message","id":"16497e3d","parentId":"03f5c09c","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:45:31.783Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test_dates` passes now. In `dates/parse.py`, `parse_date` calls `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`. That format had nothing to match the trailing `Z`, which caused the error. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass.\n\nWhat changes for callers:\n- Timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset like `+02:00` now come back timezone-aware: `...Z` gives `tzinfo=timezone.utc`, and `+02:00` gives a UTC+2 offset.\n- Timestamps with no zone still come back without a timezone, as before, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave the same.\n- It also accepts other ISO-8601 forms the old format rejected, such as fractional seconds or a bare date.\n- If any code compares these results with datetimes that have no timezone, Python raises a `TypeError`. Inside this repo the only caller is `day_key`, which isn't affected.\n- This needs Python 3.11 or later; older `fromisoformat` doesn't accept `Z`. The repo doesn't pin a version, and this machine runs 3.13.5."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":402,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":27481,"totalTokens":27885,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":27481}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277127166,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8cx23EqMuxhBWyKS1VE","duration":4592.984128,"ttft":4501.889583,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27483,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
